  "id": "script-theory",
  "term": "script theory",
  "definition": "Script theory is the idea that people use stored knowledge structures, or internal scripts, to guide how they act in collaborative learning situations. In this account, these scripts include elements such as roles, scenes, and smaller action units, and they are reorganized as people work toward their goals.",
